# Dependency install scripts are off so `npm install` works on a clean machine.
#
# better-sqlite3 ships a prebuilt binary for every platform we target (its
# prebuilds/ folder includes win32-x64, darwin-arm64, linux-x64 and friends).
# But the package also contains a binding.gyp, and npm's default install step for
# any package with a binding.gyp is `node-gyp rebuild` — so npm tries to compile
# from source and fails on a machine without a C++ toolchain:
#
#   gyp ERR! find VS  Could not find any Visual Studio installation to use
#
# That is a hard stop for anyone cloning this on Windows without Visual Studio
# Build Tools, for a binary that was already in the tarball. Skipping install
# scripts uses the prebuilt binary instead, which is what we want anyway.
#
# Verified on a clean clone: 128 tests pass and `npm run demo` serves the full
# demo world with no build tools installed.
ignore-scripts=true
